<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patrick Buchan-Hepburn, 1st Baron Hailes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a>–<a href="/years/1974">1974</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lord Hailes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Patrick Buchan-Hepburn, 1st Baron Hailes, was a British Conservative politician who served as Chief Whip and then as the only governor-general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> Federation, from 1958 to 1962. He presided over the federation from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-of-spain">Port of Spain</a> during its short life, which ended after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> voted to leave in 1961 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tobago">Tobago</a> followed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/patrick-buchan-hepburn-1st-baron-hailes.jpg" alt="Patrick Buchan-Hepburn, 1st Baron Hailes" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Glyn Warren Philpot · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patrick_Buchan-Hepburn,_Lord_Hailes,_by_Glyn_Warren_Philpot.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
